      "id": 12650,
      "name": "Estelindis",
      "username": "Estelindis",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/estelindis/{size}/2017_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-03-13T23:40:03.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>From&nbsp;1:33:45 of <a href=\"http://www.twitch.tv/greaterthangames/b/633860012\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">a recent Tactics stream from PAX</a>, there was what seemed(?) like a new ad for the video game. &nbsp;<span>(Maybe it is actually not new; I always tended to skip the gaps between matches previously, so I wouldn't have seen it if it was shown before.) &nbsp;The ad had</span><span>&nbsp;voice acting for Baron Blade, something I've never heard before. &nbsp;It was quite heavily accented. &nbsp;There was also some new art, showing Baron Blade looking at a hologram of his moonfall plan, showing estimated casualties of&nbsp;</span><span>5.8 billion people</span><span>. &nbsp;Anyway, it made me wonder if there's going to be voice acting added to the game, whether in general (<a href=\"http://handelabra.com/blog/2015/2/26/the-more-you-know-creating-an-expansion\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">maybe for the \"flavorQuotes\" value seen here?</a>) or just for the eventual campaign mode. &nbsp;Maybe extra cutscenes too, given the new art. &nbsp;Very exciting!</span></p><p>Baron Blade's voice-acted dialogue was as follows: \"<span>You claim you fight for freedom, but yours is a legacy of destruction, a legacy of death. &nbsp;It matters not who you surround yourself with, Mr. Parsons. &nbsp;No nations, no heroes, no sentinels you can assemble can hope to stand in the face of the inevitable. &nbsp;The moon is a constant reminder of the passage of time. &nbsp;Is it not fitting that now the end of your time is also the end of the moon's time? &nbsp;I will leave your world in ruins! &nbsp;Whatever remains will be mine.\"</span></p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:44:15.025Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
