      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">From&nbsp;1:33:45 of <a href=\"http://www.twitch.tv/greaterthangames/b/633860012\">a recent Tactics stream from PAX</a>, there was what seemed(?) like a new ad for the video game. &nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">(Maybe it is actually not new; I always tended to skip the gaps between matches previously, so I wouldn&#39;t have seen it if it was shown before.) &nbsp;The ad had</span><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">&nbsp;voice acting for Baron Blade, something I&#39;ve never heard before. &nbsp;It was quite heavily accented. &nbsp;There was also some new art, showing Baron Blade looking at a hologram of his moonfall plan, showing estimated casualties of&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">5.8 billion people</span><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">. &nbsp;Anyway, it made me wonder if there&#39;s going to be voice acting added to the game, whether in general (<a href=\"http://handelabra.com/blog/2015/2/26/the-more-you-know-creating-an-expansion\">maybe for the &quot;flavorQuotes&quot; value seen here?</a>) or just for the eventual campaign mode. &nbsp;Maybe extra cutscenes too, given the new art. &nbsp;Very exciting!</span></p><p style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">Baron Blade&#39;s voice-acted dialogue was as follows: &quot;<span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">You claim you fight for freedom, but yours is a legacy of destruction, a legacy of death. &nbsp;It matters not who you surround yourself with, Mr. Parsons. &nbsp;No nations, no heroes, no sentinels you can assemble can hope to stand in the face of the inevitable. &nbsp;The moon is a constant reminder of the passage of time. &nbsp;Is it not fitting that now the end of your time is also the end of the moon&#39;s time? &nbsp;I will leave your world in ruins! &nbsp;Whatever remains will be mine.&quot;</span></p>",
